  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result with the single combined bracket: fails** (superseded by Section 7). $R_B$ varies by up to $\\sim10^8$, also within weight sectors. The diagnostic below shows why: the combined bracket gives only 9 rows for 6 unknowns, and $\\det N$ then depends on the choice of rows in a state-dependent way. That holds even at $A=B$. **Fix (Paul):** at L=2 there are two brackets, one for each ladder (the insertions $1$ and $e^{2\\pi iu/h}$); see Section 7.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "rowsAlt = {{1, 3}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}, {2, 1}, {3, 1}, {1, 1}};\ndAlt = Table[Det[Table[rowF[B, \"vac\", ij], {ij, rowsAlt}]], {B, nS}];\ndSameAlt = Table[Det[Table[rowF[B, B, ij], {ij, rowsAlt}]], {B, nS}];\nspread[r_] := Max[Abs[r/r[[1]] - 1]];\nbySec = GatherBy[Range[nS], muS[[#]] &];\nchecks[\"det N row-choice ratio state-independent (mixed: B vs vac)\"] = spread[dAlt/dV];\nchecks[\"det N row-choice ratio state-independent (same twist, A=B)\"] = spread[dSameAlt/Diagonal[detZ]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"diagnostic\", \"max |ratio/ratio_1 - 1|\"},\n   {\"row choice {13,12,23,21,31,11} vs off-diagonal rows, mixed twist\", ScientificForm[N[spread[dAlt/dV], 3], 3]},\n   {\"same, same twist A=B\", ScientificForm[N[spread[dSameAlt/Diagonal[detZ]], 3], 3]}},\n  Table[{Row[{\"R_B spread in sector \", muS[[g[[1]]]], \" (\", Length[g], \" states)\"}], ScientificForm[N[spread[RB[[g]]], 3], 3]}, {g, Select[bySec, Length[#] > 1 &]}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
